  "text_pages": [
    "Exchange/Visiting Pre-Arrival Guide - d. Visa FAQ\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nFrequently Asked Questions\nVISA\nF.A.Q.\nHow long is my visa valid for?\nAs of Fall 202\n4\n, Immigration has changed their validity period policy (\nThe\nimmigration office ultimately decides the validity) for D-2-6 /\nD-2-8\napplicants as shown below:\n4 months  -\n5\nmonth visa\n6 months -\n5\nmonth visa\n10 months - 10 month visa\n12 months - 1\n0\nmonth visa\nMY RC says the expiration date is XX but HUFS says differently?\nHUFS reports the end of your studies two weeks after the last day of the semester. From then, students will have two weeks to leave the country despite the expiration date indicated on the RC when first received.\nCan I switch from a D-2-6 (Exchange) to a D-4 (Language CEnter) Visa?\nOnly if you physically leave Korea, apply for a D-4 visa and re-enter. There is no way to change without doing so. Students who wish to do this MUST consult the OIAM first.\nWhat is the longest I can have an exchange student visa for?\n12 months.\nCan I switch from an Exchange student visa to a visiting student visa (or vice versa)?\nOnly if you physically leave Korea, apply for a D-\n2-8\nvisa and re-enter. There is no way to change without doing so.\nCAN i EXTEND MY RESIDENCE CARD (RC)\n?\nLONG TERM RESIDENCE CARD\nEXTENSION\nStudents who plan on extending their term of study at HUFS must apply for an extension of their Residence Card (RC) prior to the start of their extended study period.\nThis can be completed online or through an in-person visit to the immigration office. Please keep in mind that you\nmust\nmake an appointment prior to your visit to the immigration office. There is a fee\nof KRW 50,000.\nRequired Documents:\nApplication Form\nPassport\nCertificate of Residence Card\nDocuments evidencing the applicant's place of stay\nDocuments according to each status of stay\nTEMPORARY RESIDENCE CARD EXTENSION\nStudents can apply for a\ntemporary extension\nfor their Residence Card (RC). Students may apply for an extended stay of up to 30 days once their term of study has ended. This can be completed online or through an in-person visit to the immigration office.\nRequired Documents:\nPassport\nOne copy of your airline ticket that indicates the date of departure\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nReport abuse"
  ],
